Z||000000||Darren's 87 coupe||10-28-2001||10:13 PM||||Man are these cars great or what!!!  I got mine out for the first time the other day and this morning.  Just wanted to share the excitement.  It needed a new fuel filter after 2 years of sitting and then it started up.  It's smoking and leaking oil in the water, so it's now going to sit for a while till I get some head work done, but it was fun anyway, just to feel it.  Oh well, just excited to post this finally.  Might add the 4.9 later on in the next 6 months or so.  Any one who has done it with a 5 speed let me know how it is?  Can't wait till I get to get her on the highway.  Some day soon.  Thanks for letting me ramble on.<BR>Darren||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-28-2001||10:18 PM||||Cool!  Sounds like you might have a cracked head and/or blown head gasket.  Engine swaps can be fun and challenging, but I don't think you can use a 5 speed with the caddy engine.  All the ones I've seen have used the auto out of the caddy itself, I believe.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Darren's 87 coupe||10-28-2001||10:31 PM||||I know that ed parks is selling a kit for the manuel trans as soon as feb or march, at a cost of 3200$.  A bit steep, but I would like to try it out to be a little original, but i don't think i would be the first.  I also hear  that his workmanship is worth the price.<BR>Darren||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackStang95||10-29-2001||12:44 AM||||If the engines running bad, don't bother sinking money into it.  Swap something in, be it v-8 or v-6.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Darren's 87 coupe||10-29-2001||07:43 AM||||I'm going to have to sink just a little money into it to get the 4cyl limping a long for another 6 months.  Probably just a few hundred, then, I'll be saving for the swap.  Donations are welcome to help with the v8 cause.  While it's limping, I'll be fixing anything not engine related while I save for the big engine swap.||||reg||1
